{
  "facts": [
    "Content rules in src/rules/contentLimits.ts inspect .slidev-layout roots; custom layouts must supply that class, as documented in README.md.",
    "Character counts include laid-out text even when CSS clips or clamps it; data-slidev-check-ignore is the explicit exclusion mechanism for intentionally excluded content.",
    "Text metrics inspect HTML and SVG text; direct native MathML is outside the documented scope, while Slidev's standard KaTeX HTML rendering is counted and its MathML accessibility copy is excluded.",
    "The guideline's visual ten-line budget requires manual review; automatic content checks cover body characters, list depth, and table rows, alongside the existing layout rules.",
  ],
}
